  "notes": "Four bullets and all four are load-bearing, which is unusual. The Damp Scroll earns its own obtain rung because it is the one genuinely observable thing in the quest and it is needed BEFORE the giver will talk -- bullet 2 is explicit that it must be in inventory when you speak to Shivivi. Its zone is null on purpose: the page offers fishing it up in Sea Serpent Grotto OR buying it off the auction house, and a step has one zone, so neither is asserted. The scroll is then held again for step 3, but it is evidence only on step 1 -- the same item may not mark two rungs.\n\nThe hand-in is not an NPC: you trade the scroll to the hot springs in Horlais Peak and it transforms in place. The page names the target only as 'the Hot Springs' and gives no grid for it, so that is what is recorded; whether a live entity carries that name is unverified, hence the step sits at medium. Jubaku: Ichi is the header's Reward, so it proves the quest is over and is deliberately not used as evidence on step 3. This is the oldest revision in the batch by a wide margin and the walkthrough is correspondingly thin, but it does not contradict itself.",
